Java Interface and Package Demo

This is a simple Java project created to practice interfaces, packages, and polymorphism. It contains two musical instrument classes, Veena and Saxophone, that implement a common Playable interface.

The project is useful for beginners who want to understand how Java organizes classes into packages and how interfaces help achieve abstraction and code reusability.

What this project includes

* A Playable interface with a play() method.
* A Veena class that implements the interface.
* A Saxophone class that implements the interface.
* A Test class that demonstrates method calls and interface-based polymorphism.

Concepts Used

* Java Interfaces
* Packages and Imports
* Method Overriding
* Runtime Polymorphism
* Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)

